direction: down

title: |md
  ## XDP vs tc — when to pick which
| {near: top-center; shape: text}

xdp: "XDP" {
  style.fill: "#fef3c7"
  x_body: |md
    Where: driver, before skb alloc
    Speed: ~10 ns + your logic
    Sees: raw frame bytes (data, data_end)
    Direction: ingress only
    Modify: yes (carefully — no skb metadata yet)
    Helpers: bpf_redirect, bpf_xdp_adjust_head, ...

    **Best for:** drop, forward, simple parsing
  |
}

tc: "tc / tcx" {
  style.fill: "#dcfce7"
  t_body: |md
    Where: after skb allocation (ingress)
            or before driver xmit (egress)
    Speed: ~50 ns + your logic
    Sees: __sk_buff (full kernel metadata)
    Direction: **ingress AND egress**
    Modify: yes, with skb helpers
    Helpers: bpf_skb_*, bpf_csum_diff, bpf_redirect_peer, ...

    **Best for:** policy, mark, NAT, encap, egress
  |
}

both: "Use both" {
  style.fill: "#dbeafe"
  b_body: |md
    Cilium-style: XDP for fast-path drops/loadbalance,
    tc for skb-aware filtering and egress shaping.
    The two run in **different positions** — they
    don't conflict; they compose.
  |
}

xdp -> both
tc -> both
